{"page_content": "Conversion of concentration from wet weight to dry weight soil or sediments\n\nIn this guidance the concentrations in soil and sediment are expressed on a wet weight basis. As the PNECsed and PNECsoil are expressed in dry weight, also the respective concentrations need to be expressed in dry weight.\n\nThe conversion factors CONVsoil, and CONVsusp, for soil and suspended matter respectively, are derived with the following formula:\n\nRHO comp CONV = tn7 pwn. COMP \u201c~ Fsolidcomp * RHO sotia with comp \u20ac {soil, susp}\n\nEquation R.16- 2\n\nExplanation of symbols", "metadata": {"doc_id": "3b9b266a-a09e-4601-b749-36c7685e203f", "content_type": "CompositeElement", "filename": "IR_CSR_R16_V4_FINAL.pdf"}}